  <Scene>
    <WorldInfo title="The Fastest Route Bends" info="&quot;X3D Math Lab • Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.&quot;">
      <MetadataString containerField="metadata" name="mathlab.sample" reference="mathlab.x3d/1" value="&quot;{\&quot;adapter\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.x3d/1\&quot;,\&quot;axes\&quot;:\&quot;Upper diagram uses physical x,y with interface y=0. Lower inset: horizontal q∈[0,d] mapped to display x∈[−2.5,2.5]; vertical is T(q)−Tmin (no vertical rescaling), shifted below the ray diagram by the baseline recorded in numerical data. Vacuum speed c is normalized to one.\&quot;,\&quot;bounds\&quot;:{\&quot;center\&quot;:[0.0,-1.0755654737977642,0.03749999999999999],\&quot;size\&quot;:[5.5,5.556244042355082,0.775]},\&quot;configuration_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;9fc16bf8c0f8681fc4ba4e39be9c0815bcbbeb09e194bd5024d7e131f43b81c3\&quot;,\&quot;insights\&quot;:[\&quot;Refractive indices are positive relative indices n≥1, and vacuum speed is normalized to one. Optical cost is Σnᵢ·lengthᵢ, proportional to physical travel time.\&quot;,\&quot;Cyan is the globally shortest geometric segment between the fixed points. Mint minimizes optical cost over paths crossing this flat interface once; these optimize different quantities when indices differ.\&quot;,\&quot;T″(q)=n₁h₁²/(q²+h₁²)^(3/2)+n₂h₂²/((d−q)²+h₂²)^(3/2)&gt;0. Endpoint derivatives have opposite signs, so this bounded family has one interior minimizer, located by derivative bisection rather than sampled argmin.\&quot;,\&quot;The lower cost plot has its own q axis mapped to width five and plots T−Tmin above a declared baseline placed below the physical rays, without vertical rescaling. It is not part of the physical ray geometry.\&quot;,\&quot;This fixed-source/fixed-target transmission problem does not prescribe an arbitrary incident ray. It therefore does not demonstrate a total-internal-reflection cutoff. Fermat's principle outside this convex family is a stationary-path principle, not universally a shortest-time rule.\&quot;],\&quot;lesson\&quot;:\&quot;refraction\&quot;,\&quot;metrics\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;trial_cost\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Trial optical travel cost\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;c=1 units\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:4.741513430618609},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;minimum_cost\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Minimum optical travel cost\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;c=1 units\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:4.620517378825526},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;excess\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Trial cost above minimum\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.12099605179308259},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;snell\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Snell / stationary residual\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;|n₁sin θ₁−n₂sin θ₂|; angles measured from the interface normal.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.1102230246251565e-16},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;crossing\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Optimal crossing q/d\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.7064058102105154}],\&quot;parameters\&quot;:{\&quot;crossing\&quot;:0.5,\&quot;depth\&quot;:1.2,\&quot;height\&quot;:1.1,\&quot;n1\&quot;:1,\&quot;n2\&quot;:1.5,\&quot;span\&quot;:3},\&quot;sample_schema\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.sample/1\&quot;,\&quot;sample_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;3b6a053e289d3fca27952900b9fee893107219d428e46c42a5cca226dfd3fdae\&quot;,\&quot;scope\&quot;:\&quot;Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.\&quot;,\&quot;title\&quot;:\&quot;The Fastest Route Bends\&quot;,\&quot;view\&quot;:\&quot;planar\&quot;}&quot;" />
    </WorldInfo>
